<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alexis Kagame</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1912">1912</a>–<a href="/years/1981">1981</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alexis Kagame was a Rwandan Catholic priest, philosopher, historian and poet. Given access to the royal court's ritual specialists, he recorded the dynastic poems, genealogies and esoteric code of the Rwandan kingship, publishing them from the 1940s onwards. His works on Rwandan history and on Bantu philosophy made him one of the best-known African scholars of his generation, though historians later questioned his chronology.</p></div>
